I'm talking about NH3.0j on a PC.
I think this will work, but you have to shell out while playing (say on Dlvl 4)
with the ! command, then rename your levels.nn (or bones.nn) to levels.3, ie:the
level _above_ your current. There may still be a problem using maze levels with
this method, but I died by a trickery only when my character wanted to go down
and couldn't create a new level because there already was one! If you go
_upstairs_, the game doesn't check the continuity of the levels, just uses
what's there. This leads to...

**** ABUSE WARNING





















Multiply your posessions!
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Assume a random valuable item is in your inventory slot X. Go to any down stairs
(after level 1 I think), and drop X. Go down. Shell out. You have levels.4
(your level now) and levels.3 (with item X). 
Make a copy of levels.3 
Go back to the game. Go up to get item X back. Go back down to 4. Shell out.
Copy your duplicate level to levels.3
Go back to the game and you have doubled quantities of X.

